| `import_layers.search_roots` | list of strings | `["", "src/", "tests/", "scripts/", "scripts/jobs/", "scripts/hooks/", "scripts/agent_surface/", "mcp/", "api/rest_fastapi/", "tests/integration/"]` | each `""` (the repo root) or a repo-relative directory ending in `/`, searched in order | `tests/source_tree.py` (`import_layers`, `import_edges`) | Lists where an absolute import's dotted name is looked for, first match winning, so each `import` and `from ... import` resolves to the project file it loads; a name no root holds is external and makes no edge. A root that is no list of such strings fails the gate test. | where Python itself searches at run time: a `sys.path` entry no root names stays invisible to the layer gate | always |
